# Feature 2299, 2026-11-14: the lines beside a `use` binding a built-in's
# name. Of two lines binding `sort`, the first is told the built-in's and is
# still bound, so the second is told the clash every second line is, each with
# its own `guess`; neither message is said twice. A line nothing reads is told
# both of what is wrong with it, the built-in's name and that nothing reads
# it, since deleting it is then the repair and an alias alone would leave that
# to a second build to say.
use a/sort  #~ builtin_name_taken
use b/sort  #~ module_binding_taken
use lib/len  #~ unused_binding builtin_name_taken

function main()
    print(sort.twice(1))
